        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Puebla</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">5 May 1862</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The hills of Loreto and Guadalupe overlooking the city of Puebla de los Ángeles (now Puebla), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> under General Charles de Lorencez, with 6,000 troops; the Mexican Republican Army, with Ignacio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> giving the orders on the field, in the forts held by the division of Arteaga under General Miguel Negrete.</span></div>
